//? Title: Geohash: interleaved bits, nested cells and boundary surprises
//? Subtitle: Actual coordinate bisections, exact angular resolutions and limits of double precision
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Turn a geographic coordinate into a compact string identifying a nested angular
cell. A shared prefix can locate a common cell, but nearby points can fall on
opposite sides of a split and share no prefix. Geohash alternates longitude and
latitude bits, then groups them into a base32 alphabet. This report follows an
actual first character, reproduces the original coordinate and city examples,
and derives the alternating angular shrink factors. Native cell decoding and
traces also expose a numerical limit: extra characters eventually stop shrinking
the double-precision endpoints. Explicit record admission, strict input checks
and independent exact-rational tests make those distinctions checkable.
)

\toc

> Five actual comparisons produce the first character

Start at latitude 42.6°, longitude −5.6°. The first longitude comparison chooses
the lower half of [−180,180]; the latitude comparison chooses the upper half of
[−90,90]. Three further comparisons produce the bit sequence 01101. Its alphabet
index is 13, which maps to e in 0123456789bcdefghjkmnpqrstuvwxyz. The resulting
first-character cell has longitude [−45,0] and latitude [0,45]. These values below
come from the executing native kernel, not a local report implementation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hash_first.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/geohash.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_trace(42.6,-5.6,1,7);std::string decisions;
 std::print("| bit | axis | lower before | upper before | actual midpoint | upper chosen | accumulator after |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
 for(const auto&e:t.bits){decisions+=e.upper?'1':'0';std::print("| {} | {} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {} | {} |\n",e.step,e.longitude?"longitude":"latitude",e.lower_before,e.upper_before,e.midpoint,e.upper,e.symbol_value);}
 const auto&e=t.emissions.at(0);std::print("\nActual decisions {}; emitted character {}; alphabet index {}; longitude [{:.0f}, {:.0f}]; latitude [{:.0f}, {:.0f}]; records {}.\n",decisions,e.symbol,e.symbol_value,e.bounds.lon_lo,e.bounds.lon_hi,e.bounds.lat_lo,e.bounds.lat_hi,t.captured_records);
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(63,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.3;box.height=2.3;box.font_size=22;
 d.node("point",{0,0},std::format("Input point\nlatitude = {:.1f}\nlongitude = {:.1f}",t.latitude,t.longitude),box)
  .node("bits",{6,0},std::format("Actual lon/lat decisions\n{}\nvalue = {}",decisions,e.symbol_value),box)
  .node("cell",{12,0},std::format("Emitted character: {}\nlon [{:.0f}, {:.0f}]\nlat [{:.0f}, {:.0f}]",e.symbol,e.bounds.lon_lo,e.bounds.lon_hi,e.bounds.lat_lo,e.bounds.lat_hi),box)
  .edge("point","bits","5 tests").edge("bits","cell","base32")
  .text({6,2.5},"Longitude first; alternate axes; take the upper half on equality",24).save_svg("build/hash_first.svg");
 if(decisions!="01101"||e.symbol!='e'||e.symbol_value!=13)throw std::runtime_error("first actual character");
}
