> Mathematical resolution and double endpoint resolution eventually diverge

The formulas above describe an ideal dyadic grid. The encoder instead repeatedly
stores double endpoints and computes their double midpoint. Eventually a selected
interval can remain unchanged, or its endpoints can become equal. A nonzero
unchanged interval and a collapsed interval are different events. The native
run exposes the first one-based bit index of each, using 0 when absent, and keeps
executing every requested bit and emission.

For the original coordinate, the first unchanged interval occurs at bit 110 in the
latitude updates. It remains a nonzero interval. Native longitude endpoints also
stop shrinking later. At 1024 characters, ideal angular spans round to zero in
double, while actual endpoint differences remain nonzero. At the poles/end-meridians,
actual intervals can collapse instead. Neither continued characters nor a stable
comparison means additional geographic information or a certified real-cell bound.
The decoder marks limited=true when such endpoint events occur; re-encoding its
computed center is not promised to recover an arbitrarily long degenerate key.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hash_precision.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/geohash.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_trace(42.6,-5.6,32,193);std::vector<double>x,actual_lon,actual_lat,ideal_lon,ideal_lat;
 for(const auto&e:t.emissions){const auto ideal=dm::algorithms::geohash_resolution(int(e.characters));const double w=e.bounds.lon_hi-e.bounds.lon_lo,h=e.bounds.lat_hi-e.bounds.lat_lo;if(w<=0||h<=0||!ideal.spans_positive)throw std::runtime_error("positive plotting domain");x.push_back(e.characters);actual_lon.push_back(std::log10(w));actual_lat.push_back(std::log10(h));ideal_lon.push_back(std::log10(ideal.longitude_degrees));ideal_lat.push_back(std::log10(ideal.latitude_degrees));}
 std::print("| characters | actual longitude span | actual latitude span | ideal longitude span | ideal latitude span | first unchanged bit | decoder limited |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
 for(int p:std::array<int,8>{1,5,12,20,22,24,32,1024}){const auto r=dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_run(42.6,-5.6,p);const auto c=dm::algorithms::geohash_decode(r.hash);const auto ideal=dm::algorithms::geohash_resolution(p);std::print("| {} | {:.6e} | {:.6e} | {:.6e} | {:.6e} | {} | {} |\n",p,c.longitude_span,c.latitude_span,ideal.longitude_degrees,ideal.latitude_degrees,r.first_unchanged_bit,c.limited);}
 const auto longrun=dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_run(42.6,-5.6,1024),pole=dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_run(90,180,32);
 std::print("\nOriginal coordinate: first unchanged bit {}; first collapsed bit {}; actual bisections {}; emitted characters {}. Pole/end-meridian first collapsed bit {}; final latitude span {:.6e}; final longitude span {:.6e}.\n",longrun.first_unchanged_bit,longrun.first_collapsed_bit,longrun.work.bisections,longrun.work.emissions,pole.first_collapsed_bit,pole.bounds.lat_hi-pole.bounds.lat_lo,pole.bounds.lon_hi-pole.bounds.lon_lo);
 auto lon=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();lon.lines(x,actual_lon,"Actual",{37,99,235},2).lines(x,ideal_lon,"Ideal dyadic",{220,38,38},2).legend({"Actual","Ideal dyadic"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}}).title("Longitude: actual and ideal").xlab("Characters").ylab("log10 positive angular span").y_limits(-25,4);
 auto lat=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();lat.lines(x,actual_lat,"Actual",{37,99,235},2).lines(x,ideal_lat,"Ideal dyadic",{220,38,38},2).legend({"Actual","Ideal dyadic"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}}).title("Latitude: actual and ideal").xlab("Characters").ylab("log10 positive angular span").y_limits(-25,4);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(lon).add(lat).size(1100,500).title("Extra characters eventually stop refining double endpoints").fit_panels().save_svg("build/hash_precision.svg");
 if(longrun.first_unchanged_bit!=110||longrun.first_collapsed_bit||longrun.work.bisections!=5120||!pole.first_collapsed_bit)throw std::runtime_error("actual endpoint limits");
}
