> Complete histories, strict inputs and ownership

An encoder trace retains one initial coordinate/bounds record, 5p actual bit
records and p actual emission records. Its exact complete count is

$$
H(p)=1+6p.
$$
\alttext(One initial coordinate and bounds record plus five bit records and one emission record per requested character gives one plus six p complete records.)

Admission checks this whole bound, vector capacities and a positive quota before
initialization/history allocation. Default cap is one million records; zero disables
only that optional quota. These are complete fixed-schema records, not numeric
entries or bytes, and this is not a peak RAM limit. Final ordinary output, root/work
metadata, working state and allocator storage are excluded. Stagnation receives
no early-stop discount. There is no numerical replay, truncation, partial returned
trace or caller mutation on rejection. A zero-character trace still has its one
initial record. Ordinary encoding uses O(p) output bytes and O(1) other state;
complete history adds O(p) records. No arbitrary positive precision cap is imposed
on the scalar API, subject to representable counters and available storage.

Legacy valid-coordinate negative precision, including INT_MIN, retains zero-length
compatibility. New checked run/trace/resolution counts reject negatives. All
coordinate calls reject nonfinite/out-of-range values before work, even when a
zero or negative legacy count would return empty. Decoder and prefix utilities
validate the entire strict alphabet before arithmetic/comparison, including an
invalid trailing byte beyond an already different first character. Empty decoding
means the world; input is not silently lowercased or wrapped at the date line.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hash_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/geohash.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 bool denied=false,negative=false,nonfinite=false,bad_key=false,large=false;
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_trace(42.6,-5.6,5,30);}catch(const std::length_error&){denied=true;}auto t=dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_trace(42.6,-5.6,5,31);const auto final=t.run.hash;t.bits[0].midpoint=999;t.emissions[0].bounds.lat_hi=999;t.initial_bounds.lon_lo=999;const bool owned=t.run.hash==final&&t.bits[1].midpoint!=999&&t.emissions[1].bounds.lat_hi!=999&&t.run.bounds.lat_hi!=999;
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_trace(0,0,-1,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){negative=true;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_trace(std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(),0,0,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){nonfinite=true;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::geohash_common_prefix("0","z!");}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){bad_key=true;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_trace(0,0,std::numeric_limits<int>::max(),1);}catch(const std::length_error&){large=true;}
 const auto zero=dm::algorithms::geohash_encode_trace(42.6,-5.6,0,1);const auto world=dm::algorithms::geohash_decode("");
 std::print("| resource | required | captured | rejected cap | rejection observed |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Five-character complete trace | {} | {} | 30 | {} |\n| Zero-character initial record | {} | {} | 0 (quota off) | false |\n",dm::algorithms::geohash_trace_records(5),t.captured_records,denied,dm::algorithms::geohash_trace_records(0),zero.captured_records);
 std::print("\nIndependent owned records {}; negative checked count before quota {}; nonfinite coordinates before quota {}; full alphabet checked despite differing first character {}; huge trace rejected before allocation {}; legacy INT_MIN key empty {}.\n",owned,negative,nonfinite,bad_key,large,dm::algorithms::geohash_encode(0,0,std::numeric_limits<int>::min()).empty());
 std::print("Empty key: world longitude span {:.0f} degrees; latitude span {:.0f} degrees; center ({:.0f}, {:.0f}); actual zero-count bisections {}; emissions {}.\n",world.longitude_span,world.latitude_span,world.latitude,world.longitude,zero.run.work.bisections,zero.run.work.emissions);
 auto records=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({31.,double(t.captured_records),30.},{"Required","Captured","Rejected cap"});records.title("Whole trace admission").xlab("").ylab("Complete records, not bytes").y_limits(0,40);
 auto work=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(t.run.work.longitude_steps),double(t.run.work.latitude_steps),double(t.run.work.emissions)},{"Longitude","Latitude","Emissions"});work.title("Actual five-character work").xlab("").ylab("Axis steps or character appends").y_limits(0,17);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(records).add(work).size(1100,500).title("History records and executed encoder operations have different units").fit_panels().save_svg("build/hash_controls.svg");
 if(!denied||!owned||!negative||!nonfinite||!bad_key||!large)throw std::runtime_error("trace and input contracts");
}
