// result_end
\caption(Five characters need 31 complete records and perform 13 longitude tests,12 latitude tests and 5 emissions. The huge-count check exercises trace admission only; it does not run a huge scalar encoding or impose that trace quota on scalar calls.)
\alttext(Two panels show 31 required/captured records versus rejected cap 30 and actual work counts 13 longitude steps,12 latitude steps and 5 emissions. Computed controls include zero-count/world decoding and independent record ownership.)

The native trace preserves the original encoded keys while explaining what their
characters mean. Shared prefixes give nested angular cells; boundary examples
refute the proximity converse. Exact bit counts explain alternating angular
resolutions, and actual endpoint flags expose the gap between an ideal grid and
finite arithmetic. These constant-coordinate and generated-cell experiments need
no external dataset or timing benchmark, and make no physical-distance guarantee
from a string prefix alone.
